	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9ea85fcce56f3bd3","type":"group","x":-440,"y":200,"width":3400,"height":2260,"color":"1","label":"Appo11y"},
		{"id":"9b0709194d423571","type":"group","x":-420,"y":700,"width":3360,"height":1700,"color":"2","label":"Instrumenter"},
		{"id":"cb5fbe77a92ea5ec","type":"text","text":"pkg/components/beyla.go\n\n**Function RunBeyla**\n```\nRunBeyla(context.Context, *beyla.Context) error\n```\n- check whether application monitoring, networking monitoring or both are enabled.\n- calls `setupOlly`.\n\n**Function SetupO11y**\n\n```\nsetupO11y(context.Context, global.ContextInfo, *beyla.Config)error\n```\n- Calls `apolly.New()`.","x":-120,"y":-600,"width":860,"height":580},
		{"id":"a1f1355020eb5205","type":"text","text":"cmd/beyla/main.go\n\n**main Function**:\n- do something with configuration.\n- there is something called the pprof http listener.\n- calls `components.RunBeyla`\n\n","x":-780,"y":-470,"width":545,"height":330},
		{"id":"5cf6cc6d436d8ad7","type":"text","text":"# Instrumenter\n\nThere are overall two types of instrumenters, `AppO11y` and internal, `pipe` Instrumenter. They look like these.\n\n## Apo11y Instrumenter\n\n```go\n// Instrumenter finds and instrument a service/process, and forwards the traces as\n// configured by the user\ntype Instrumenter struct {\n\tconfig    *beyla.Config\n\tctxInfo   *global.ContextInfo\n\ttracersWg *sync.WaitGroup\n\tbp        *pipe.Instrumenter\n\n\t// tracesInput is used to communicate the found traces between the ProcessFinder and\n\t// the ProcessTracer.\n\ttracesInput *msg.Queue[[]request.Span]\n}\n```\n\n## Pipe Instrumenter\n```go\ntype Instrumenter struct {\n\tinternalMetrics imetrics.Reporter\n\tgraph           *swarm.Runner\n}\n```\n\n`Appo11y` instrumenter has two important things we need to understand:\n- bp\n- tracesInput\n\ntraces input is a queue, that contains `request.Span` type values. It has two important methods.\n- `FindAndInstrument`\n- `ReadAndForward`\nBut even before these methods are triggered, the Instrumenter pipeline contains multiple nodes, which are built by the `New` method. The pipeline contains many components, but the starting happens from the `traceinput` queue, which does next steps.\n\nThese pipeline components are actually ground together using a `swarm.Instancer`, which creates and instantiates the graph, along with handling errors in creation.\n\nThe main focus point is the `traceInput`.\n### FindAndInstrument\n`FindAndInstrument` keeps checking the system for executable programs matching a criteria. It depends on the `discover.ProcessFinder` which looks like this.\n\n```go\ntype ProcessFinder struct {\n\tcfg         *beyla.Config\n\tctxInfo     *global.ContextInfo\n\ttracesInput *msg.Queue[[]request.Span]\n}\n```\nhere, the `tracesInput` is the same channel being used as input by the reader and `decorater` pipeline.\n\nThe entire thing starts with `ProcessFinderFunc`.\n\n#### ProcessWatcherFunc\nThis is the data structure on which the entire thing depends.\n\n```go\ntype pollAccounter struct {\n\tcfg      *beyla.Config\n\tinterval time.Duration\n\t// last polled process:ports accessible by its pid\n\tpids map[PID]processAttrs\n\t// last polled process:ports accessible by a combination of pid/connection port\n\t// same process might appear several times\n\tpidPorts map[pidPort]processAttrs\n\t// injectable function\n\tlistProcesses func(bool) (map[PID]processAttrs, error)\n\t// injectable function\n\texecutableReady func(PID) (string, bool)\n\t// injectable function to load the bpf program\n\tloadBPFWatcher func(cfg *beyla.Config, events chan<- watcher.Event) error\n\tloadBPFLogger  func(cfg *beyla.Config) error\n\t// we use these to ensure we poll for the open ports effectively\n\tstateMux          sync.Mutex\n\tbpfWatcherEnabled bool\n\tfetchPorts        bool\n\tfindingCriteria   services.DefinitionCriteria\n\toutput            *msg.Queue[[]Event[processAttrs]]\n}\n```\n\nThe data being handled at this point is `Event` made of `processAttr` structs, which looks like this.\n```go\ntype processAttrs struct {\n\tpid       PID\n\topenPorts []uint32\n\tmetadata  map[string]string\n\tpodLabels map[string]string\n}\n```\n\nIt starts with and also contains `loadBPFWatcher` function.\n","x":880,"y":-3000,"width":1240,"height":1960},
		{"id":"1109dcf69f17864b","type":"text","text":"pkg/internal/apolly/apolly.go\n\n**Function New**\n\n```go\nNew(context.Context, *global.ContextInfo, beyla.Config)(Instrumenter, error)\n```\n- [ ] setupFeatureContextInfo()\n- [ ] `tracesInput: msg.Queue[[]Request.Span]]`\n- [ ] pipe.Build(): something Happens to traceInput\n","x":-420,"y":220,"width":1000,"height":420},
		{"id":"43d94d12753dcaf8","type":"text","text":"pkg/internal/pipe/instrumenter.go\n\n**Function Build**\n```go\nfunc Build(ctx context.Context, config *beyla.Config, ctxInfo *global.ContextInfo, tracesCh *msg.Queue[[]request.Span]) (*Instrumenter, error) {\n\treturn newGraphBuilder(config, ctxInfo, tracesCh).buildGraph(ctx)\n}\n```\n\n**Function newGraphBuilder**\n```go\n func newGraphBuilder(config *beyla.Config, ctxInfo *global.ContextInfo, tracesCh *msg.Queue[[]request.Span]) *graphFunctions {}\n```\n- Initializes a `swarm.Instancer{}`.\n- Initialize a `graphFunctions` object.\n- Add `traces.ReadFromChannel(*ReadDecorator)`\n\t- [ ] Add definition of `ReadDecorator` here.\n\t- Input: `tracesCh`.\n\t- Output: `tracesReaderToRouter`.\n\t- Function:\n\t\t- Subscribe to `tracesCh`.\n\t\t- For every `traceinput` from `tracesCh`\n\t\t\t- decorate it\n\t\t\t- send it out on `tracesReaderToRouter`.\n\t\t- [ ] Understand how the pipeline stops in cascade mode.\n- Add `transform.RoutesProvider()`.\n\t- Input: `tracesReaderToRouter`.\n\t- Output: `routerToKubeDecorator`.\n\t- Function:\n\t\t- [ ] To Find Out.\n- Add `transform.KubeDecoratorProvider()`.\n\t- Input: `rouerToKubeDecorator`\n\t- Output: `kubeDecoratorToNameResolver`\n\t- Function:\n\t\t- [ ] To Be Done.\n- Add `transform.NameResolutionProvider()`.\n\t- Input: `kubeDecoratorToNameResolver`. \n\t- Output: `nameResolverToAttrFilter`.\n\t- Function:\n\t\t- [ ] To be Done.\n- Add `filter.ByAttribute`\n\t- Input: `nameResolverToAttrFilter`.\n\t- Output: `exportableSpans`.\n\t- Function:\n\t\t- [ ] To be Done.\n","x":-400,"y":720,"width":1500,"height":1660},
		{"id":"0551df60755a947c","x":1100,"y":720,"width":1540,"height":1020,"type":"text","text":"## FindAndInstrument"}
